{"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftPreprocessing\/documentation\/SwiftPreprocessing\/HardwareRouterAndMemory"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftPreprocessing\/documentation\/SwiftPreprocessing"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Understand how SwiftSci automatically routes workloads between CPU (Accelerate\/AMX\/NEON) and Metal GPU (MLX) with strict concurrency safety."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Apple Silicon features a ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Unified Memory Architecture (UMA)"}]},{"text":" where the CPU, GPU, and Apple Neural Engine (ANE) share a single high-bandwidth memory pool. ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiftPreprocessing","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" provides intelligent hardware routing and memory reservation primitives to prevent GPU saturation and avoid data copying.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"1-The-Hardware-Router","text":"1. The Hardware Router","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HardwareRouter"},{"type":"text","text":" assesses tensor dimensions and operation complexity to select the optimal computing engine:"}]},{"code":["graph TD","    Op[Compute Operation] --> Router{HardwareRouter}","    Router -->|Small \/ Vector < 50k| CPU[Accelerate \/ AMX \/ NEON]","    Router -->|Large Matrix \/ Autodiff| GPU[MLX Metal GPU]","    Router -->|Static Inference| ANE[Core ML Engine]"],"syntax":"mermaid","type":"codeListing"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Small Vectors (","type":"text"},{"code":"N < 50,000","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":")","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Routed to CPU Accelerate (vDSP\/BLAS\/LAPACK) to eliminate GPU kernel dispatch latency."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Large Tensors & Deep Learning","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Routed to MLX Metal GPU for massive parallel throughput."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"2-WiredMemoryManager--Ticket-System","text":"2. WiredMemoryManager & Ticket System","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To prevent out-of-memory (OOM) conditions during concurrent analytical workloads, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WiredMemoryManager"},{"type":"text","text":" implements an asynchronous FIFO reservation system:"}]},{"code":["import SwiftPreprocessing","","\/\/ Acquire a GPU execution slot","let ticket = try await WiredMemoryManager.shared.reserveMemory(estimatedBytes: 64 * 1024 * 1024)","","\/\/ Execute heavy MLX operations","\/\/ ...","","\/\/ Automatically flushes GPU caches upon completion","await ticket.release()"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}]}],"kind":"article","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftpreprocessing\/hardwarerouterandmemory"]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftPreprocessing\/documentation\/SwiftPreprocessing\/HardwareRouter","doc:\/\/SwiftPreprocessing\/documentation\/SwiftPreprocessing\/WiredMemoryManager","doc:\/\/SwiftPreprocessing\/documentation\/SwiftPreprocessing\/WiredMemoryTicket"],"anchor":"Memory--Routing-APIs","title":"Memory & Routing APIs"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"API Collection","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Hardware Routing & Unified Memory Governance","modules":[{"name":"SwiftPreprocessing"}]},"references":{"doc://SwiftPreprocessing/documentation/SwiftPreprocessing/WiredMemoryManager":{"kind":"symbol","title":"WiredMemoryManager","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"actor"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WiredMemoryManager","kind":"identifier"}],"identifie